// Title: UAC Bypass Using Consent and Comctl32 - File
// Sigma ID: 62ed5b55-f991-406a-85d9-e8e8fdf18789
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-23 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass using consent.exe and comctl32.dll (UACMe 22)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_uac_bypass_consent_comctl32.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\consent.exe.@" and FolderPath endswith "\\comctl32.dll"
